1
00:01:30,260 --> 00:01:34,880
Episode 9

2
00:01:30,260 --> 00:01:34,880
Episode 9

3
00:01:30,260 --> 00:01:34,880
The Misanthrope and the Heart's Deepest Desire

4
00:01:30,260 --> 00:01:34,880
The Misanthrope and the Heart's Deepest Desire

5
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:34,970
Director's Office

6
00:01:34,660 --> 00:01:36,710
What do you think of the advanced class?

7
00:01:37,140 --> 00:01:38,770
It hasn't been without its trouble,

8
00:01:39,090 --> 00:01:42,630
but things have settled down 
since Ohgami decided on her career path.

9
00:01:42,630 --> 00:01:43,500
That's good.

10
00:01:44,230 --> 00:01:46,420
Now it's your turn, Haneda.

11
00:01:47,020 --> 00:01:48,090
Me?

12
00:01:48,670 --> 00:01:49,270
Yeah.

13
00:01:49,790 --> 00:01:52,350
What do you want to do 
after you become human?

14
00:01:52,740 --> 00:01:55,090
Make music, I suppose.

15
00:01:55,090 --> 00:01:56,060
Really?

16
00:01:56,570 --> 00:01:58,850
I'd say I'm about half-serious.

17
00:01:58,850 --> 00:02:01,020
And the other half?

18
00:02:01,650 --> 00:02:04,250
I want to live life 
like you do, Mr. Hitoma.

19
00:02:04,950 --> 00:02:06,860
Are you messing with me?

20
00:02:06,860 --> 00:02:10,050
You've got plenty 
to enjoy in life, don't you?

21
00:02:10,570 --> 00:02:12,600
Indulging your passions into the night.

22
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:15,780
Don't say it like that! 
I'm just going to play video games!

23
00:02:16,470 --> 00:02:20,980
I want to create things 
that I love, just like you do.

24
00:02:21,580 --> 00:02:25,950
There may be setbacks, 
but I know they'll help me grow kinder.

25
00:02:26,760 --> 00:02:28,300
Just like you, Mr. Hitoma.

26
00:02:29,310 --> 00:02:31,880
I wouldn't call myself very kind.

27
00:02:32,250 --> 00:02:33,740
Sure you are.

28
00:02:34,070 --> 00:02:37,370
In my eyes, you come off as very human.

29
00:02:38,060 --> 00:02:40,890
What does "human" even mean here?

30
00:02:41,460 --> 00:02:43,440
How you're not perfect.

31
00:02:43,440 --> 00:02:46,100
Mr. Hitoma, have you ever gotten angry?

32
00:02:46,100 --> 00:02:47,070
Yeah.

33
00:02:47,070 --> 00:02:48,350
Any bad memories?

34
00:02:48,710 --> 00:02:50,190
Plenty of them.

35
00:02:50,430 --> 00:02:52,080
What about happy ones?

36
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:53,760
Plenty of those, too.

37
00:02:53,760 --> 00:02:55,440
Painful memories?

38
00:02:55,440 --> 00:02:56,710
Lots of them.

39
00:02:56,710 --> 00:02:58,250
Times you've given up?

40
00:02:58,630 --> 00:03:00,990
I give up on something every day.

41
00:03:01,310 --> 00:03:03,080
Times you've been sad?

42
00:03:03,900 --> 00:03:05,370
More than I can remember.

43
00:03:06,070 --> 00:03:10,730
There are all sorts of emotions 
that have brought color to your life.

44
00:03:11,210 --> 00:03:14,710
All of them are what 
make you who you are now.

45
00:03:16,310 --> 00:03:18,410
I have plenty of things I regret, too.

46
00:03:21,010 --> 00:03:22,190
Say, Mr. Hitoma.

47
00:03:22,190 --> 00:03:23,060
What is it?

48
00:03:23,390 --> 00:03:27,220
If you could face your regrets, 
would you give them your best?

49
00:03:27,820 --> 00:03:28,810
What's that mean?

50
00:03:28,810 --> 00:03:30,590
Just a hypothetical.

51
00:03:30,590 --> 00:03:33,210
Would you rather forget your regrets?

52
00:03:33,210 --> 00:03:34,950
Or face them head-on?

53
00:03:36,510 --> 00:03:37,910
Well...

54
00:03:38,390 --> 00:03:41,240
If I could do everything over...

55
00:03:42,770 --> 00:03:45,830
I'd want to face them... I think.

56
00:03:46,610 --> 00:03:47,570
I see.

57
00:03:47,930 --> 00:03:50,380
Mr. Hitoma, you've grown stronger.

58
00:03:51,690 --> 00:03:53,220
It'd be nice if that was the case.

59
00:03:55,250 --> 00:03:58,920
It's time once again 
for the advanced class final assignments.

60
00:03:59,300 --> 00:04:03,610
To graduate and become human, 
you'll have to pass your final assignment.

61
00:04:04,210 --> 00:04:06,210
Everyone gets a different assignment.

62
00:04:06,630 --> 00:04:08,590
Please give it your all.

63
00:04:09,590 --> 00:04:13,610
How come I'm the only 
one who got this big box?!

64
00:04:13,910 --> 00:04:15,630
What is that?

65
00:04:17,160 --> 00:04:19,430
My final assignment.

66
00:04:19,430 --> 00:04:21,120
It's shattered into pieces.

67
00:04:21,810 --> 00:04:25,270
Machi broke it because 
she's rash and reckless.

68
00:04:26,270 --> 00:04:28,310
She's already failed her assignment.

69
00:04:28,630 --> 00:04:30,320
Nuh-uh!

70
00:04:30,320 --> 00:04:33,630
My assignment is 
to repair this with kintsugi!

71
00:04:34,020 --> 00:04:37,380
Oh, they have assignments like that?

72
00:04:38,180 --> 00:04:40,280
What about you, Uchami?

73
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:44,780
I have to write letters 
to everyone in the advanced class.

74
00:04:44,780 --> 00:04:47,010
What? That's a piece of cake!

75
00:04:47,010 --> 00:04:49,770
You'll be done writing that in no time!

76
00:04:49,770 --> 00:04:50,900
Not fair!

77
00:04:51,310 --> 00:04:52,810
Be a little more serious.

78
00:04:52,810 --> 00:04:55,420
Even if I write down whatever, 
it won't be graded well.

79
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:57,320
Guess you're right.

80
00:04:58,230 --> 00:05:01,940
On top of the final assignment, 
I need to study to get into med school.

81
00:05:02,390 --> 00:05:04,000
I have so much on my plate.

82
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:07,810
You even have Mr. Hoshino 
helping you study after school.

83
00:05:08,610 --> 00:05:10,920
What's the assignment for you two, Ohgami?

84
00:05:11,490 --> 00:05:13,830
A-As for me...

85
00:05:14,350 --> 00:05:20,130
I need to write reviews for ten works, 
which include novels, comics, and essays.

86
00:05:20,620 --> 00:05:22,130
Ten of them?!

87
00:05:22,550 --> 00:05:28,480
<i>The Tale of Genji,</i> Kafka's <i>Metamorphosis,</i> 
and much more, even American comic books.

88
00:05:29,990 --> 00:05:32,400
What'd you get as an assignment, Ryuzaki?

89
00:05:32,650 --> 00:05:37,440
I have to take on the dorm 
mother Ryouko's work for ten days.

90
00:05:37,440 --> 00:05:39,930
Really? That sounds rough.

91
00:05:39,930 --> 00:05:43,160
I hear Ryouko will be away for ten days.

92
00:05:43,160 --> 00:05:44,910
I'll be taking over during that time.

93
00:05:45,510 --> 00:05:48,690
So you have to cook for the dorms?

94
00:05:48,690 --> 00:05:50,510
There's more to it than that.

95
00:05:50,510 --> 00:05:52,710
She also looks after the beginner class,

96
00:05:52,710 --> 00:05:56,160
not to mention cleaning, laundry, 
all sorts of small tasks...

97
00:05:56,160 --> 00:05:59,130
And dealing with whatever 
problems pop up, too.

98
00:05:59,130 --> 00:06:01,800
Sounds like a heavy workload.

99
00:06:02,070 --> 00:06:04,570
I wonder if I'll be able to handle it.

100
00:06:04,970 --> 00:06:08,330
You'll do just fine, Karin. Good luck.

101
00:06:08,330 --> 00:06:10,390
Thank you, Tobari!

102
00:06:10,660 --> 00:06:15,200
I'll think of it as practice 
for when I marry Mr. Rei!

103
00:06:15,200 --> 00:06:16,840
S-Sure...

104
00:06:17,330 --> 00:06:20,180
What's your assignment, Tobari?

105
00:06:20,180 --> 00:06:23,550
I have to make a musical 
instrument by hand.

106
00:06:23,790 --> 00:06:25,550
A musical instrument by hand?

107
00:06:25,550 --> 00:06:26,970
What are you going to make?

108
00:06:27,540 --> 00:06:29,300
That's a good question.

109
00:06:29,300 --> 00:06:31,460
You haven't decided yet?

110
00:06:31,460 --> 00:06:34,680
Nope, but I think it'll be fun.

111
00:06:37,380 --> 00:06:40,660
That's looking pretty big. 
What are you making?

112
00:06:40,660 --> 00:06:45,720
An electric guitar. 
I was thinking of making it a Les Paul.

113
00:06:46,350 --> 00:06:50,100
Can one person even make 
an electric guitar?

114
00:06:50,650 --> 00:06:53,290
They sell guitar necks 
with the frets and all,

115
00:06:53,720 --> 00:06:57,860
as well as parts like pegs, 
bridges, and all the circuitry.

116
00:06:57,860 --> 00:07:00,030
I see. It's totally beyond me!

117
00:07:01,330 --> 00:07:03,540
This sure is a squeaking pain.

118
00:07:03,540 --> 00:07:06,110
Traditional craft? More like a puzzle!

119
00:07:06,360 --> 00:07:08,480
Shut up, Machi!

120
00:07:08,480 --> 00:07:13,080
Squeak! Tobari's woodworking's 
way louder than me!

121
00:07:13,570 --> 00:07:16,350
That's part of her assignment, 
so I don't mind it.

122
00:07:16,930 --> 00:07:19,800
Hey! Stop playing favorites!

123
00:07:21,190 --> 00:07:23,500
Looks like Ohgami's busy reading.

124
00:07:24,610 --> 00:07:26,720
What's that you're reading, Ryuzaki?

125
00:07:27,130 --> 00:07:29,750
A manual for performing 
dorm mother duties.

126
00:07:30,130 --> 00:07:33,640
Ryouko wrote down all the important parts.

127
00:07:34,210 --> 00:07:37,310
Ryouko's as reliable as ever, I see.

128
00:07:37,310 --> 00:07:49,390
Shiranui High
Student Dorm Manual

129
00:07:37,650 --> 00:07:41,980
She even wrote down tips for dealing 
with all of the beginner class students.

130
00:07:42,620 --> 00:07:46,020
All the students at this school 
are way too quirky!

131
00:07:46,020 --> 00:07:48,940
You're pretty quirky yourself, Ryuzaki.

132
00:07:52,530 --> 00:07:56,420
Your guitar's really starting 
to take shape after a week.

133
00:07:56,420 --> 00:07:59,050
Mr. Hitoma, listen to this!

134
00:07:59,050 --> 00:08:00,740
Karin's such a meanie!

135
00:08:00,740 --> 00:08:02,520
Give her a good lecture!

136
00:08:02,520 --> 00:08:07,010
Hey, Machi. Crying 
to Mr. Rei is playing dirty.

137
00:08:07,560 --> 00:08:08,890
What happened?

138
00:08:08,890 --> 00:08:11,890
She won't let me have seconds when I eat!

139
00:08:11,890 --> 00:08:12,470
What?

140
00:08:12,710 --> 00:08:15,280
The budget doesn't allow for it.

141
00:08:15,280 --> 00:08:17,790
I can't go against the rules.

142
00:08:17,790 --> 00:08:21,380
Isn't it your job 
to make all of that work out?

143
00:08:21,380 --> 00:08:23,820
You're a no-good crooked magistrate!

144
00:08:24,400 --> 00:08:27,110
Shut up already!

145
00:08:27,580 --> 00:08:28,780
Usami?

146
00:08:29,750 --> 00:08:32,000
I-I'm sorry.

147
00:08:35,460 --> 00:08:37,090
Don't mind me.

148
00:08:37,430 --> 00:08:39,620
You just took me by surprise...

149
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:44,750
It's my fault.

150
00:08:47,690 --> 00:08:48,490
Usami!

151
00:08:49,340 --> 00:08:50,380
Sorry, Haneda.

152
00:08:50,380 --> 00:08:52,400
Wrap up the rest of class for me.

153
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:53,810
Got it!

154
00:08:57,910 --> 00:08:59,340
Mr. Hitoma.

155
00:09:01,480 --> 00:09:03,600
Ms. Karasuma.

156
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:06,350
Usami's in the nurse's office.

157
00:09:10,750 --> 00:09:11,790
Usami.

158
00:09:12,570 --> 00:09:14,360
I'm awful.

159
00:09:15,560 --> 00:09:16,970
I get annoyed easily.

160
00:09:17,540 --> 00:09:19,100
I have angry outbursts.

161
00:09:20,130 --> 00:09:22,170
I made Isaki cry...

162
00:09:24,440 --> 00:09:31,320
I'm sorry. I was the one making 
the most trouble in class.

163
00:09:32,540 --> 00:09:34,180
It's fine.

164
00:09:34,700 --> 00:09:36,630
What's fine about that?

165
00:09:37,080 --> 00:09:42,860
Everyone has times when dealing 
with others gets to be too much.

166
00:09:42,860 --> 00:09:43,990
I know that.

167
00:09:44,890 --> 00:09:46,390
That's right.

168
00:09:47,470 --> 00:09:51,650
You'll feel calmer 
after a nice, warm drink.

169
00:09:53,590 --> 00:09:54,870
It's good.

170
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:57,540
Glad to hear it.

171
00:09:58,780 --> 00:10:02,210
I'll apologize when I go back 
to the classroom.

172
00:10:02,550 --> 00:10:03,180
Yeah.

173
00:10:03,670 --> 00:10:06,630
I'm sorry I didn't warn them 
about being too loud.

174
00:10:07,130 --> 00:10:09,310
Yeah, you should be.

175
00:10:10,050 --> 00:10:12,140
Looks like you're feeling a bit better.

176
00:10:12,550 --> 00:10:13,910
Usami.

177
00:10:13,910 --> 00:10:16,680
Thanks for putting 
the nurse's office to good use.

178
00:10:17,370 --> 00:10:21,980
I'm always here, so feel free 
to drop by whenever you need.

179
00:10:22,580 --> 00:10:26,660
Haruka, why'd you decide 
to become a school nurse?

180
00:10:27,640 --> 00:10:32,820
I wanted to give people 
a place to run away to.

181
00:10:33,370 --> 00:10:35,350
A place to run away to?

182
00:10:35,900 --> 00:10:39,530
You get people like that, 
who work a little too hard.

183
00:10:41,420 --> 00:10:43,080
Don't look at me like that.

184
00:10:45,010 --> 00:10:49,130
It's always better to have 
more places you can turn to.

185
00:10:50,020 --> 00:10:52,240
Advanced Class

186
00:10:59,940 --> 00:11:03,330
What? Stop staring at me.

187
00:11:03,330 --> 00:11:08,130
I see you're working on your 
assignment instead of studying.

188
00:11:08,520 --> 00:11:09,900
Making good progress?

189
00:11:10,450 --> 00:11:12,950
I'm not cut out 
for this kind of assignment.

190
00:11:13,500 --> 00:11:16,760
It should have been 
a writer like Isaki who does this.

191
00:11:17,820 --> 00:11:22,930
Isn't the point of the assignment 
for you to get over not being good at it?

192
00:11:23,560 --> 00:11:25,240
I know that already.

193
00:11:25,240 --> 00:11:27,540
I was complaining, 
not asking for an explanation.

194
00:11:28,520 --> 00:11:29,790
How about you, Machi?

195
00:11:30,230 --> 00:11:32,770
I'm glad you asked.

196
00:11:32,770 --> 00:11:38,610
Believe it or not, today will be the final
step for my dear Bowledoodle!

197
00:11:38,830 --> 00:11:41,640
Huh? Bowl-a-what now?

198
00:11:41,640 --> 00:11:43,090
Bowledoodle!

199
00:11:43,090 --> 00:11:46,410
The name of the bowl 
I've been looking after!

200
00:11:50,760 --> 00:11:53,690
<i>Looks like Ohgami's struggling.</i>

201
00:11:57,930 --> 00:11:59,500
There we go!

202
00:11:59,500 --> 00:12:00,920
I think I'm all done!

203
00:12:00,920 --> 00:12:03,150
You really made a guitar?

204
00:12:03,730 --> 00:12:05,500
The wood grain looks so cool.

205
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:09,850
This is my first time seeing 
an electric guitar in person!

206
00:12:28,020 --> 00:12:30,970
You play that thing really well, Haneda.

207
00:12:31,860 --> 00:12:32,970
Really?

208
00:12:33,910 --> 00:12:35,590
Thanks, Mr. Hitoma.

209
00:12:35,910 --> 00:12:38,950
I'm off to go submit it to the principal!

210
00:12:41,110 --> 00:12:43,610
It's so cool that she can play 
an instrument.

211
00:12:44,180 --> 00:12:48,020
Mr. Rei, do you like girls 
who can play instruments?

212
00:12:48,260 --> 00:12:53,020
Oh, it's more that I respect 
people who are multi-talented.

213
00:12:53,020 --> 00:12:55,710
I see. I learned something new!

214
00:12:55,710 --> 00:12:58,260
Thanks, Mr. Rei! I love you!

215
00:13:00,500 --> 00:13:02,550
Again with the immoral displays.

216
00:13:02,550 --> 00:13:04,390
You're working hard, too, Usami.

217
00:13:04,780 --> 00:13:06,630
I'll do it since I've been asked to.

218
00:13:07,390 --> 00:13:11,210
But Isaki must be a real masochist 
to do this every day.

219
00:13:11,210 --> 00:13:12,580
Wh-What?!

220
00:13:16,230 --> 00:13:18,180
E-Excuse us.

221
00:13:19,130 --> 00:13:23,050
Oh? You're from the beginner class.

222
00:13:24,470 --> 00:13:27,800
Karin! Thanks for everything 
over the past ten days!

223
00:13:28,360 --> 00:13:30,450
Thank you!

224
00:13:30,980 --> 00:13:33,650
Th-Thanks...

225
00:13:36,660 --> 00:13:39,730
Oh! Those are so cute!

226
00:13:39,730 --> 00:13:45,220
They asked me to teach them 
how to make icing.

227
00:13:46,070 --> 00:13:49,580
So this is what they were trying to make.

228
00:13:50,730 --> 00:13:56,090
I didn't get to see it, but looks 
like you did just fine as dorm mother.

229
00:13:56,500 --> 00:13:58,930
Yes, of course.

230
00:14:00,840 --> 00:14:03,600
Nezu, how's your assignment going?

231
00:14:03,600 --> 00:14:06,570
Squeak! I-I'll submit it sooner or later.

232
00:14:06,570 --> 00:14:10,370
Didn't you say you were 
on the last step yesterday?

233
00:14:11,270 --> 00:14:13,270
How come you remember that?

234
00:14:13,270 --> 00:14:14,870
Don't click your tongue at me!

235
00:14:14,870 --> 00:14:21,210
But once I submit it, 
Bowledoodle's gonna be gone!

236
00:14:21,770 --> 00:14:25,970
Huh? You usually get to 
keep it afterwards.

237
00:14:25,970 --> 00:14:28,160
Wait, really?

238
00:14:28,160 --> 00:14:31,370
Yeah. I got to keep this guitar.

239
00:14:31,370 --> 00:14:34,790
Well now I feel stupid 
for worrying so much.

240
00:14:37,350 --> 00:14:39,150
How's it going, Ohgami?

241
00:14:39,150 --> 00:14:43,410
W-Well, I do have a good 
deal of it sorted out...

242
00:14:44,070 --> 00:14:45,010
What's up?

243
00:14:45,470 --> 00:14:48,840
I wonder if these reviews are good enough.

244
00:14:49,400 --> 00:14:53,930
I can't help but worry that 
I may have misinterpreted something.

245
00:14:54,900 --> 00:14:57,160
Everyone gets something 
different out of art.

246
00:14:57,770 --> 00:15:00,650
You should write down exactly 
how you feel about them.

247
00:15:01,110 --> 00:15:03,830
Yes, but still...

248
00:15:08,510 --> 00:15:10,810
Isaki's report is straight-up fire!

249
00:15:10,810 --> 00:15:13,030
She's so good at tying it all together!

250
00:15:13,030 --> 00:15:14,200
Isaki.

251
00:15:15,030 --> 00:15:17,370
Help me with my assignment.

252
00:15:17,370 --> 00:15:19,870
Huh? You don't mean Isaki?

253
00:15:20,470 --> 00:15:24,960
My assignment is to write a letter 
for everyone in the advanced class.

254
00:15:25,210 --> 00:15:28,460
You mean I'm included in that?

255
00:15:29,020 --> 00:15:30,300
Of course you are.

256
00:15:30,660 --> 00:15:34,580
If I miss my chance today, I have to 
wait a month, which will be too late.

257
00:15:34,580 --> 00:15:36,560
So I wrote yours first.

258
00:15:39,390 --> 00:15:41,080
Ushami!

259
00:15:41,080 --> 00:15:44,010
H-Hey! Get your grubby mitts off me!

260
00:15:44,010 --> 00:15:45,690
Isaki, sit!

261
00:15:47,690 --> 00:15:49,160
No hesitation!

262
00:15:49,560 --> 00:15:54,270
Just keep in mind that I'm not 
as good at writing as Isaki.

263
00:15:54,270 --> 00:15:57,230
Writing letters isn't about 
how good or bad you are!

264
00:15:57,230 --> 00:15:58,850
I'm so happy!

265
00:15:58,850 --> 00:16:01,670
Hey, can I read it now? 
I don't think I can wait!

266
00:16:02,610 --> 00:16:03,900
S-Sure...

267
00:16:03,900 --> 00:16:07,530
It's yours now, so I can't stop you.

268
00:16:07,530 --> 00:16:10,270
Sweet! Thanks!

269
00:16:10,580 --> 00:16:12,090
Let's see...

270
00:16:21,560 --> 00:16:23,710
Thanks, Ushami...

271
00:16:23,710 --> 00:16:29,090
This stuff about my bright, cheery smile 
or how you think I'm considerate...

272
00:16:29,090 --> 00:16:33,250
I really appreciate all 
the good things you wrote about me!

273
00:16:33,250 --> 00:16:37,950
I'm <i>so</i> happy you feel that way, Ushami!

274
00:16:35,820 --> 00:16:38,540
I told you to get your hands off me!

275
00:16:38,910 --> 00:16:42,380
I <i>love</i> you lots too, Ushami!

276
00:16:42,380 --> 00:16:46,460
I know we don't see each other often, 
but I'm glad you still remembered me!

277
00:16:46,460 --> 00:16:47,970
Thanks, Ushami!

278
00:16:47,970 --> 00:16:51,840
How could I forget someone so annoying?

279
00:16:51,840 --> 00:16:54,480
What? Guess I'll have to be more annoying!

280
00:16:54,480 --> 00:16:55,960
Shut up!

281
00:16:55,960 --> 00:16:59,260
I can't wait for my letter from Usami.

282
00:16:59,260 --> 00:17:02,020
When will I be getting mine?

283
00:17:02,830 --> 00:17:04,360
I'm looking forward to it!

284
00:17:05,700 --> 00:17:10,910
Usami, you use simple words 
that directly convey how you feel.

285
00:17:10,910 --> 00:17:13,360
Your writing is so thoughtful and sweet.

286
00:17:13,360 --> 00:17:15,620
I really love it.

287
00:17:16,630 --> 00:17:19,590
I've never gotten a letter before.

288
00:17:19,590 --> 00:17:22,650
It's like your words 
are coming alive on paper.

289
00:17:22,650 --> 00:17:24,520
How wonderful.

290
00:17:25,450 --> 00:17:30,000
I can tell that you pay close attention 
to both me and yourself.

291
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:34,840
I've always admired 
how you never admit defeat.

292
00:17:36,770 --> 00:17:38,220
Uchami...

293
00:17:40,330 --> 00:17:42,540
Why'd you burst into tears?

294
00:17:42,940 --> 00:17:46,670
I never knew that's how you felt about me!

295
00:17:46,670 --> 00:17:51,860
Man, you really love me, don't you?!

296
00:17:52,110 --> 00:17:55,130
Machi, please don't cry.

297
00:17:55,130 --> 00:17:57,960
If you start crying, I...

298
00:17:58,870 --> 00:18:01,750
I won't be able to stop myself, either!

299
00:18:01,980 --> 00:18:05,320
Hey, don't you go crying now, Isaki.

300
00:18:05,740 --> 00:18:08,870
I've been holding back this whole time!

301
00:18:09,580 --> 00:18:12,010
What? Karin, too?

302
00:18:12,010 --> 00:18:14,650
Hah! Usami made them cry!

303
00:18:15,150 --> 00:18:17,680
Tobari! Don't make me 
sound like the bad guy!

304
00:18:17,950 --> 00:18:21,440
It really is all your fault, Usami...

305
00:18:21,440 --> 00:18:26,150
After always being so stern, 
you're so kind in your letter...

306
00:18:26,150 --> 00:18:28,820
She's right! What's the big idea?

307
00:18:28,820 --> 00:18:30,570
You're head over heels for me!

308
00:18:30,570 --> 00:18:33,800
You didn't have to say all 
those nice things about me!

309
00:18:34,580 --> 00:18:37,270
Cry or get angry, pick one!

310
00:18:40,200 --> 00:18:43,000
Hitoma. This is my last letter.

311
00:18:43,500 --> 00:18:45,000
I get one, too?

312
00:18:45,230 --> 00:18:48,890
Everyone in the advanced 
class includes you, Hitoma.

313
00:18:49,330 --> 00:18:52,750
I'm not gonna fall 
for a simple trick question like that.

314
00:18:54,030 --> 00:18:54,950
Also...

315
00:18:55,780 --> 00:18:59,310
Neneko Kurosawa

316
00:18:56,180 --> 00:18:58,500
This is for Neneko.

317
00:18:59,850 --> 00:19:03,030
She was a student this 
school year, so...

318
00:19:04,270 --> 00:19:05,620
Thanks, Usami.

319
00:19:06,120 --> 00:19:08,350
I'll deliver this letter for you.

320
00:19:08,770 --> 00:19:09,930
Thanks.

321
00:19:09,930 --> 00:19:12,090
Not gonna read yours?

322
00:19:12,090 --> 00:19:13,860
I'll do it when I get home.

323
00:19:13,860 --> 00:19:16,490
What? Why not now?

324
00:19:16,780 --> 00:19:20,340
Nope. I bet I'll cry when I do.

325
00:19:21,270 --> 00:19:22,680
I guess that's true.

326
00:19:22,680 --> 00:19:24,750
I've made up my mind.

327
00:19:25,460 --> 00:19:28,790
All this time, I've been worried 
about the reviews for my assignment.

328
00:19:29,480 --> 00:19:32,540
But thanks to Usami's letter, 
I've seen the light.

329
00:19:33,530 --> 00:19:38,230
Instead of stressing out over details, 
I need to plainly state the way I feel.

330
00:19:38,680 --> 00:19:42,250
That's all I need to do in order 
to stir people's emotions.

331
00:19:43,140 --> 00:19:45,410
Hurry up and finish 
your assignment, Isaki.

332
00:19:45,810 --> 00:19:47,600
I know you can do it.

333
00:19:48,090 --> 00:19:50,620
Yes! Thank you!

334
00:20:04,860 --> 00:20:07,060
I'm done...

335
00:20:07,710 --> 00:20:10,730
Good work! I know it must have been hard!

336
00:20:10,730 --> 00:20:12,750
Thank you very much.

337
00:20:12,750 --> 00:20:13,870
Nice going.

338
00:20:13,870 --> 00:20:15,030
Good job.

339
00:20:15,030 --> 00:20:17,220
Ichaki, you're amazing!

340
00:20:17,890 --> 00:20:21,820
Th-Thank you, everyone...

341
00:20:23,180 --> 00:20:25,010
Ohgami, good work.

342
00:20:25,740 --> 00:20:27,030
You did your best.

343
00:20:27,480 --> 00:20:28,730
Mr. Hitoma.

344
00:20:29,370 --> 00:20:31,010
Thank you!

345
00:20:31,400 --> 00:20:33,940
Advanced class!

346
00:20:33,940 --> 00:20:36,130
A hearty congratulations to all of you!

347
00:20:36,930 --> 00:20:38,530
Principal.

348
00:20:38,530 --> 00:20:44,250
I've just confirmed that you've all 
completed your graduation assignments.

349
00:20:44,250 --> 00:20:50,990
After careful consideration, we've decided
who meets the graduation requirements!

350
00:20:51,940 --> 00:20:54,440
The students graduating this year...

351
00:20:54,770 --> 00:20:56,470
are more diligent than the rest,

352
00:20:56,470 --> 00:20:59,810
care greatly for others, 
and show deep passion for their interests.

353
00:20:59,810 --> 00:21:06,020
Faced with doubts and hardship, 
they persevered as a pair, hand-in-hand.

354
00:21:06,830 --> 00:21:11,980
Cheerful and kind, 
they learned to love themselves.

355
00:21:11,980 --> 00:21:14,040
And for their graduation assignment,

356
00:21:14,040 --> 00:21:18,060
from the words and ideas of tales old 
and new, from around the world,

357
00:21:18,060 --> 00:21:20,570
they learned to communicate, 
or in other words,

358
00:21:20,570 --> 00:21:26,570
express their thoughts and feelings 
with greater precision than before.

359
00:21:29,750 --> 00:21:34,230
For these reasons stated, 
this year's graduating students...

360
00:21:35,100 --> 00:21:39,540
Isaki Ohgami and Isaki Ohgami.

361
00:21:39,540 --> 00:21:41,150
It'll be you two.

362
00:21:42,200 --> 00:21:46,470
Once again, congratulations!

363
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:50,600
Thank you very much.

364
00:21:58,380 --> 00:22:01,380
Thank you, everyone!

365
00:23:32,990 --> 00:23:40,020
Next Episode:

366
00:23:32,990 --> 00:23:40,020
The Misanthrope and the Comet's Pilgrimage

